  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@bright-y/dsh-restart",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nOne-click restart button for DeepSeek Harness: a circular-arrow button in the\nconversation header's right-side utilities area (next to \"Session log\") that\nrelaunches DSH Desktop gracefully after confirmation. No more closing and\nreopening the app by hand after installing plugins."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "- A bordered capsule button at the top-right of the session header (matching\n  the header's own controls and the app theme).\n- Clicking it opens a confirm dialog (restart is disruptive — running\n  sessions, tasks and unsaved state may be interrupted).\n- Confirming POSTs to the loopback-only `/api/dsh-restart/restart` route; the\n  host relaunches DSH Desktop via `desktopActions.requestRestart`\n  (Electron `app.relaunch`) a beat after the acknowledgement.\n- On a plain `dsh web` boot (no desktop shell) the route answers 501 and the\n  button explains that one-click restart requires DSH Desktop."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "After installing, restart `dsh web` and the restart button appears in the\nsession header."
    },
    {
      "section": "From this repository (git)",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add git+https://github.com/bright-y/dsh-restart.git#main\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From the release package (.tgz)",
      "text": "Download `dsh-restart-0.1.0.tgz` from the\n[Releases](../../releases) page, then:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add /path/to/dsh-restart-0.1.0.tgz\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From the repository (development)",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/bright-y/dsh-restart.git\ncd dsh-restart\npnpm install\npnpm run build"
    },
    {
      "section": "Security model",
      "text": "- The host API is loopback-only: requests from non-local addresses, foreign\n  Host headers and cross-site origins are rejected with 403.\n- The restart route only exists in a DSH Desktop shell; on other runtimes it\n  answers 501 without touching the host."
    },
    {
      "section": "Known limitations",
      "text": "- One-click restart requires DSH Desktop (the Electron shell). On plain\n  `dsh web` the button reports that the runtime is unsupported.\n- Restart interrupts the current process; any running session/task is\n  suspended and resumes after relaunch."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Apache-2.0."
    }
  ],
